-- title:
--   Every element of the crossing model is a constant mod 𝔪
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative local ring and let $\pi \in W$ be a non-unit. Write $M =$ `UVCrossingModel W π` for the quotient of the ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ of formal power series in two variables (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - C(\pi)$, and assume $M$ is local. For `w : W`, `const π w` denotes the class in $M$ of the constant series $C(w)$. The assertion is that for every $x \in M$ there exists $w \in W$ such that $x -$ `const π w` lies in the maximal ideal of $M$. Equivalently, the composite $W \to M \to M/\mathfrak m_M$ is surjective, so the residue field of the crossing model is that of $W$.
--
--   The crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi)$ is the standard local model for a node, e.g. for the completed local ring of a modular curve at a supersingular point in characteristic dividing the level; this lemma is the "every element is congruent to a constant" input used downstream, for instance in the length and pullback computations for node annuli ([`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.finsum_finrank_quotient_eq_length_of_comap_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.finsum_finrank_quotient_eq_length_of_comap_eq) and the statements identifying completed stalks with crossing models).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_sub_const_mem_maximalIdeal.lean

